{
  "chapter": "HV_HIGH_VOLTAGE",
  "description": "§aPolytetrafluoroethylene (PTFE)§r is a §7Carbon§r-§bFluorine§r polymer. Similarly to PVC, PTFE can be used to increase the yield of Plastic Circuit Boards and other crafts. Presently, it is used to make the walls of §3Large Chemical Reactors§r.

§3Chlorine§r is required in the process, which is fully recycled if you electrolyze the §aHydrochloric Acid§r waste.

§bFluorine§r will also be used in the §aUranium§r and §7Naquadah§r refinement processes.",
